// MULTILINE STRING scaffolds.
//
// A multiline string is the one construct in TJSON you cannot type in a single
// motion: the closing fence belongs on its own line, at exactly one legal
// column, and the parser rejects the document until both fences exist. So it is
// the one construct worth a snippet.
//
// WHY THE CLOSING FENCE LANDS RIGHT WITHOUT ANY BOOKKEEPING
//
// Two facts do it between them. The closing fence sits at the construct's
// structural indent + 1 -- a constant, at every depth, not a function of
// nesting. And VS Code prepends the current line's leading whitespace to every
// snippet line after the first. So one literal space in front of the closing
// fence is correct whether the key is at indent 2, 4, or 20, and the snippet
// never has to know which.
//
// WHY THERE IS NO ``` SCAFFOLD HERE
//
// That same prepending is why the transparent form cannot be a snippet. Its
// body is raw -- indentation in front of a body line IS part of the string --
// so VS Code indenting the body to match the key would silently prepend those
// spaces to the content. The other two forms are immune: the `` form's `| `
// margin is stripped wherever it sits, and the ` form's content indent is
// defined as n+2 and stripped at exactly that width. Scaffolding ``` needs a
// plain edit from the extension, which does no indentation normalisation.
//
// Both bodies open with two content lines rather than one, so what lands is
// already a legal document -- the specification requires a multiline string to
// hold at least one real linefeed, and one body line has none.
{
	"Multiline string (bold)": {
		"prefix": ["multiline", "``"],
		"body": [
			"``",
			"| $1",
			"| $2",
			" ``$0"
		],
		"description": "Bold multiline string. The '| ' margin makes every body line visibly part of the string and keeps leading spaces in the content unambiguous."
	},
	"Multiline string (minimal)": {
		"prefix": ["multiline-minimal", "`"],
		"body": [
			"`",
			"  $1",
			"  $2",
			" `$0"
		],
		"description": "Minimal multiline string. Body sits at n+2 with no margin -- the quietest of the three forms to read."
	}
}
